      "summaries": {
        "en": "PM Skills is an open-source marketplace of over 100 agentic skills, commands, and plugins designed to supercharge product managers with AI. It covers the full product lifecycle—from discovery and strategy to execution, launch, and growth. Technically, it provides reusable, composable skill modules that integrate with AI assistants like Claude, enabling PMs to automate tasks like user research, roadmap planning, and A/B testing. You can browse, install, and customize these skills to fit your workflow, or contribute your own to the community.",
        "zh": "PM Skills 是一个开源的产品管理技能市场，汇集超100个智能代理技能、命令和插件，覆盖产品发现、战略制定、执行、发布和增长全生命周期。其核心设计理念是将重复性工作模块化，通过可复用技能组件与Claude等AI助手无缝集成。例如，可一键调用用户访谈分析技能提炼洞察，或使用路线图规划技能生成优先级建议。技术亮点在于技能的“可组合性”，不同技能可像乐高拼接形成定制化工作流。产品经理无需从头编写提示词，直接安装社区验证技能即可提升效",
        "es": "PM Skills is an open-source marketplace of over 100 agentic skills, commands, and plugins designed to supercharge product managers with AI. It covers the full product lifecycle—from discovery and strategy to execution, launch, and growth. Technically, it provides reusable, composable skill modules that integrate with AI assistants like Claude, enabling PMs to automate tasks like user research, roadmap planning, and A/B testing. You can browse, install, and customize these skills to fit your workflow, or contribute your own to the community.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "pm-skills stands out for agent-skill-repository, agent-skills, and agentic-skills in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "PM Skills is an open-source marketplace of over 100 agentic skills, commands, and plugins designed to supercharge product managers with AI. It covers the full product lifecycle—from discovery and strategy to execution, launch, and growth. Technically, it provides reusable, composable skill modules that integrate with AI assistants like Claude, enabling PMs to automate tasks like user research, roadmap planning, and A/B testing. You can browse, install, and customize these skills to fit your workflow, or contribute your own to the community.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/phuryn/pm-skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
