      "summaries": {
        "en": "Skills is an open-source Python library by Google that provides pre-built agent skills for integrating with Google products and technologies. It simplifies building conversational agents by offering modular, reusable components for tasks like accessing Google Calendar, Gmail, or Maps. The key technical insight is its skill-based architecture, which allows developers to compose complex agent behaviors from discrete, testable units. Practically, you can use Skills to quickly prototype agents that interact with Google services, extend it with custom skills, or contribute new ones to the community.",
        "zh": "Skills 是 Google 开源的 Python 库，提供预置的 Google 产品技能模块，用于构建对话代理。它通过模块化设计将日历、邮件、地图等操作封装为可复用单元，解决从零集成 Google 服务的痛点。技术亮点在于技能架构：每个技能独立可测试，开发者可像搭积木般组合出复杂代理行为。可直接调用现有技能快速搭建原型，或编写自定义技能扩展功能，如用几行代码让代理读取 Gmail 或创建日历事件。适合需快速集成 Google 服务的 AI 应用开发者，尤其适用于个人助手或企业自动化工具。",
        "es": "Skills is an open-source Python library by Google that provides pre-built agent skills for integrating with Google products and technologies. It simplifies building conversational agents by offering modular, reusable components for tasks like accessing Google Calendar, Gmail, or Maps. The key technical insight is its skill-based architecture, which allows developers to compose complex agent behaviors from discrete, testable units. Practically, you can use Skills to quickly prototype agents that interact with Google services, extend it with custom skills, or contribute new ones to the community.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "skills stands out for google, googlecloud, and skills in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Skills is an open-source Python library by Google that provides pre-built agent skills for integrating with Google products and technologies. It simplifies building conversational agents by offering modular, reusable components for tasks like accessing Google Calendar, Gmail, or Maps. The key technical insight is its skill-based architecture, which allows developers to compose complex agent behaviors from discrete, testable units. Practically, you can use Skills to quickly prototype agents that interact with Google services, extend it with custom skills, or contribute new ones to the community.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/google/skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
