      "summaries": {
        "en": "WhichLLM is a CLI tool that helps you find the best local LLM for your specific hardware by running real benchmarks, not just comparing parameter counts. It automatically tests models via Ollama or Hugging Face, ranks them by performance and recency, and outputs a clear leaderboard. Use it to quickly identify which model runs fastest and most accurately on your Mac, GPU, or CPU, saving hours of manual trial and error.",
        "zh": "WhichLLM 是一款命令行工具，用于在本地硬件上自动测试并排名大语言模型的实际运行速度与效果。它不依赖参数数量或宣传数据，而是通过真实基准测试，在 Ollama 或 Hugging Face 上运行模型，并基于性能和时效性生成排行榜。用户只需一条命令即可测试多个模型，特别适用于 Apple Silicon、GPU 或 CPU 上的本地推理优化，快速筛选最适合设备的模型，避免手动试错。技术亮点在于“感知时效的基准测试”设计，确保推荐结果基于最新模型，可集成到开发流程中或用于比较不同量化版本（如 GGUF）",
        "es": "WhichLLM is a CLI tool that helps you find the best local LLM for your specific hardware by running real benchmarks, not just comparing parameter counts. It automatically tests models via Ollama or Hugging Face, ranks them by performance and recency, and outputs a clear leaderboard. Use it to quickly identify which model runs fastest and most accurately on your Mac, GPU, or CPU, saving hours of manual trial and error.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "whichllm stands out for ai, apple-silicon, and benchmarks in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "WhichLLM is a CLI tool that helps you find the best local LLM for your specific hardware by running real benchmarks, not just comparing parameter counts. It automatically tests models via Ollama or Hugging Face, ranks them by performance and recency, and outputs a clear leaderboard. Use it to quickly identify which model runs fastest and most accurately on your Mac, GPU, or CPU, saving hours of manual trial and error.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Andyyyy64/whichllm for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
